WEBVTT

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.580
You're sure it's this carriage, right?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.410
Yeah.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.050
I handled the arrangements for that carriage.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.220
The guy said he was going to
do something big and make tons of money.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.300
What kind of guy was he?

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.100
Give me fifty and I'll talk.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.750
Take advantage of us, will you?

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.410
Good morning.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.870
Ah, you.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.580
We don't have scoops for you.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.990
So, Lieutenant Malvin still hasn't...

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.420
No comments.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.920
No interviews for you either.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.110
Come on now, go home, go home.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.340
Okay, I'll go.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.770
But, just one thing.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:46.040
You do know that the father of tanks,
Dr. Colt, has died, right?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.880
And why are you asking about that?

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:59.050
I've heard you have visited the professor before.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.970
You know the professor?

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.250
I just met him yesterday, a year since we last met.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.210
He died later,

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.230
and I had a bad feeling...

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.830
Bad feeling?

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:08.840
Corporal Oland isn't here yet?
Bad feeling?

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.010
Corporal Oland isn't here yet?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.790
He went to search for Alice.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.210
He was very worried about her.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.510
I see.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.830
The reason I went to see the professor was the door knocker.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.850
All right, get in.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.080
Thanks.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.730
Mr. Dalton,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.890
in the beginning, even I wanted to know who he was...

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.540
...and suspected his background;

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.570
I tried to find out everything about him.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.630
And then?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.060
Did you?

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.370
Nope.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.440
We're squad mates.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.940
Knowing his background wouldn't change anything.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.020
To be suspicious of a squad mate,

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.890
you need to become one first.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.550
Now, that's your problem.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:59.830
The people in this country have a right to know their country's actions.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.780
Something as ridiculous as a foot soldier taking out a tank...

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.890
...actually took place in reality, right?

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.890
When you're in a big name newspaper,

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.230
you push yourself more than you have to, don't you?

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.070
It's my job to let the people know.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:18.320
That bad feeling you felt after meeting with Dr. Colt...

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.330
...might come to you, you know?

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.520
That's like an indirect way of saying
the professor's death was not an accident, you know?

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.530
I'm worrying about your safety.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.290
What becomes public may not be the truth.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.960
That's how both our workplaces operate, right?

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.690
Of course, no one's going to believe that a foot soldier dispatched a tank to begin with, anyway.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.230
So Invisible 9 was your work?

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:50.090
My, and what makes you say that?

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.100
I just felt like saying that.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.350
Who the hell would believe that?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:05.070
If it gets out to the public,
how many heads up top are going to fall?

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:10.010
It's my policy to not get near trouble.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.240
An intelligent decision.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:16.320
Please maintain your stance in the future, as well.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.640
There are people that stay protected because they are ignorant.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.270
Don't you think so?

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:28.170
Not at all.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.530
Knowledge can be a weapon.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.820
Your thinking just sounds like escaping.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.430
Am I wrong?

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.410
Alice!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.490
LT!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.920
Sorry for worrying you guys.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.520
You're safe.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.570
What happened?

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.730
Looks like I'd better excuse myself.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.140
Pardon me.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.700
The objective of the people that kidnapped me...

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:06.120
...was to make public a certain manuscript using Section III's powers.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.390
Manuscript?

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:11.720
One about the Invisible 9, information classified by the army.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.020
Damn it, what's happening... one person after another...

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.230
Sergeant Major Oreld.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.830
Oh, Mr. Reporter.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.170
We found one!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.030
Found one?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.120
By the way, Corporal Oland,

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.620
could I have a moment with you sometime in the future?

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.210
For what?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.280
I'll let you know.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.400
So, what did you find, Sergeant Major?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.110
A clue to the lieutenant's kidnapping.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.690
Wonderful!

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.020
You searched all night?

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:48.170
Yeah... I'm so damn sleepy right now...

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.970
And... where's that manuscript?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.210
They still have it.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.630
Now that's dangerous.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.410
We better protect them soon.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.180
We might have more corpses to handle depending on the situation.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.970
I'm amazed that you were just let go.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.610
Boss, we found a clue!

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:05.900
Ah...

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.120
Lieutenant!

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.560
LT?

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.040
You... came back?

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.910
But that reporter just...

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.810
Yeah, I just met him here.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.150
That bastard.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.200
He acted as if he didn't know.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.730
Hello, I'm-

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:58.020
I was following the scoop on the disappearance of Section III's Lieutenant Malvin,

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.040
but boy was I surprised...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.370
...that it was tied to the other scoop I was tracking down.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.000
Scoop?

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.240
Invisible 9.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.170
Hey, I talked it over with Rick, too,

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.440
but we don't have to rely on a noble like her.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.610
I mean, this guy's a reporter for the newspaper.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.640
Give him that manuscript and it'll be tomorrow's front page.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.900
Isn't that what you wanted?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.770
And he's saying he'll buy it from us at a good price.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.630
We can buy whatever we want from now on.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.800
Your brother will be happy that way.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:33.900
What's the matter, Cecile?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.320
What guarantee do I have that he'll put it in?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.400
Of course, he will!

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.040
They're a big newspaper!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.540
Sorry, but I don't trust the paper.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.040
The paper's linked with the army.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.160
That's why they used Section III.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.640
Aren't you contradicting yourself?

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.620
You hate them, no?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:56.380
I just want to put your brother's manuscript to good use.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:57.970
Go back.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.550
I'll never sell this.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:04.350
You didn't have to do that...

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.230
You're going to give us a good price, right?

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.100
We'll disappear right afterwards.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.990
You do what you want with it.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.290
Where did you get this manuscript?

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.190
I can't tell you my source.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:30.740
It'll be able to make the printing, right?

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.770
It's a big scoop,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.510
so I think we should be careful with it.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.130
Why?!

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.360
I even confirmed living proof of the Invisible 9.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.980
Then we'll put him in the article, as well.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.060
I'll wait for you until the deadline,

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.710
so get me the material that will give this article more meat.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.180
I'm your man!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:51.140
It will be tomorrow's front page!

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.230
Wait for me!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.140
You called?

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.310
I need to get in contact with somewhere urgently...

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.000
Top priority.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.850
Master, did Bruno and Rick come by?

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:20.270
No, what are they up to?

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.750
A reporter came by during the day,

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:25.280
and now, soldiers.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.260
Soldiers?

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.230
Did you get that guy?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.200
What's the matter?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.070
She's injured.

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:45.080
We have to treat it immediately.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.400
Leave me alone!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.220
Wait.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.900
Who do you mean by "that guy"?

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.330
That reporter!

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:51.970
That's so dirty of you!

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.970
For all those whitewash you said, in the end, you use money to take care of things!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.090
Isn't that cheap?!

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.660
So he went after all...

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.320
How shameless of you...

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.080
Did you let him know of the manuscript?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.420
I don't have it anymore!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:07.020
That bastard used his mouth and tricked Bruno and Rick into the deal.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.940
See? Just like I said, soldier.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.790
They said they wanted to make a fortune.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.390
It's not about the money.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:18.610
I just wanted to expose this country's corruption!

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.820
Your treatment comes first right now.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:38.900
Rick!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.070
You okay?

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:41.780
Hey!

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:44.450
Hey!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.000
It's an urgent message.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.760
Get this to the captain ASAP.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.640
Okay, this should do it.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.830
Those two were my brother's best friends...

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.980
Do people's hearts change that quickly?

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.870
You said it yourself.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.340
"Fill our stomachs with food right now!"

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:35.290
That's all there is to it.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.650
Mercury left for the HQ, right?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:38.450
Yes, sir.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.150
We need to get our hands on Dalton no matter what.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.740
Why are you... smiling?

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:49.620
I have taken in all of your feelings.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.810
What are you talking about...

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.330
You are feeling the pain of the times.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.000
I do, too.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.240
You might have planned on using Section III,

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.630
but for me,

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.990
those were words that came from a person with strong feelings for war relief,

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:06.290
and they touched me.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:10.140
I'm not going to let you sway me with those words.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:14.320
You tried to stand up for those people in the slums...

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.630
...because you couldn't stand seeing their pain and suffering, right?

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.470
Your brother's manuscript was no more than a reason for you.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.980
You obtained us, Section III, as your means.

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.690
You understand our pain?

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.490
I don't try to understand,

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:29.780
but I imagine it.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:35.520
Such irony.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:38.790
I hated you,

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.620
yet I'm counting on you.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.290
I will get back your manuscript.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:44.210
Count on us.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.430
I'm sorry we threatened you with your sisters.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:50.780
Everyone has their way of doing things.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:51.720
Don't worry about it.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.940
Hey, Cecile.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.950
That reporter came again.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:08.700
Hey.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.450
I thought I could see you again if I came here.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.500
We were just looking for you.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.240
You want it back? Now that's unexpected.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.700
Once we publicize this, I'll even let
the public know of your brother's name...

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.670
...as the person that got his hands on this scoop.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.350
You're so driven by your ambitions...

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.180
...aren't you forgetting something important?

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:39.150
What kind of impact will that bring to
the people once they learn of the news?

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:40.270
Have you thought about that?

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.570
I won't deny the ambition part,

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:46.430
but that manuscript has the power to move the nation.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.150
And the enemy will move, as well.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.590
In order to push for that war,

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.300
the army manipulated their way with public opinion.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.820
There's no way you wouldn't know that.

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.370
I understand, but...

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:02.210
Publicizing the manuscript will only bring those involved in this together even more strongly,

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.460
and the ones that are most affected by that result...

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.040
...are without doubt, the people.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.620
The more they protect and hide themselves,

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.540
the more impoverished the lives of the people will become.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.340
Isn't the wartime situation the best proof of that?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.790
The time to use that manuscript will come.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.500
I beg of you to wait until then.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.830
We aren't prepared for anything yet.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.880
But you are prepared.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.610
What?

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.610
The person that can prove the Invisible 9-

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.500
Corporal, take Cecile and run!

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:37.220
Yes, sir!

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.180
Come on! Hurry!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.670
Cecile!

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:21.170
Corporal!

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.140
Lieutenant...

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.310
Get her away... quickly...

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.720
Please!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:37.380
Run!

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.370
Hurry!

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:44.760
That's...

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.250
Corporal!

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.260
Wait!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:26.920
Who are you?

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.150
What organization do you work for?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:35.740
Why did he...

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:38.320
There was poison in his back teeth.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:43.010
Spies used it a lot on secret missions during the war.

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:44.370
Corporal!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.840
I'll get you to the hospital right away.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.040
I'm all right...

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.010
Please get the manuscript...

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:52.090
If it gets published,

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:55.950
the future you pictured will fade away, right?

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.270
Thank you, Corporal.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.320
To the newspaper office!

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:02.120
Let's go!

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.110
Captain!

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:07.950
We came right away after reading your memo,

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.310
but we're too late.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.310
Too late?

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.170
It disappeared?

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:13.900
What do you mean, it disappeared?

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:16.160
We're really sorry.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:20.830
Plus, we just received news that Dalton got killed.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:23.870
So we're really confused right now.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:24.800
You liar!

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.900
I knew the paper was with the army!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.530
You all worked together to erase my brother's manuscript!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.630
You're working with the assassins, too, right?!

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.240
Stop it, Cecile.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:35.700
Investigate this more thoroughly!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.640
It must be somewhere!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.950
We looked for it many times,

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.200
but I don't know...

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:45.430
...how much can you believe that manuscript...

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:49.110
My brother put his life on the line to find the truth,

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:53.440
that the army was doing human experiments and was turning humans into weapons of war!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.990
Really, look for the manuscript!

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.380
You say something, too, Alice!

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:07.190
We were at the scene where reporter Dalton was killed.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:13.580
We know there are people behind the scenes who want to protect that secret.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:18.920
That is the best evidence to show that the article speaks the truth.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:30.560
First, cheers for the safety of my princess.

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:39.450
But how daring of them to kidnap a soldier.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:41.400
Looking back on this incident,

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:44.410
wouldn't you say that the people are getting ripe?

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.580
Or perhaps,

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.200
to say this country is ready to leave its slumping post-war times...

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.440
...and is getting close to rebirth...

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:57.330
...or would that be too stimulating a way of putting it?

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:09.060
Here.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.000
We lost...

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.070
The two people we're looking for...

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.320
We found their corpses.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.080
Bruno and Rick?!

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.490
I apologize... for not being able to help you.

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:35.170
Everything... is lost...

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:38.000
But I'm not going to be defeated.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.370
Sometimes I'll back down.

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:41.900
Sometimes I'll accept giving up...

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.730
...for the eventual victory.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.140
What about my feelings...

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:53.080
I remember explaining the meaning of Pumpkin Scissors in the article.

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.590
Yes.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:56.320
When I came up with that name,

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:57.900
I was not afraid of anything.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:01.040
I thought I could change the world through Section III.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:04.090
Yet, as I fought with reality,

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:07.410
I was made to realize how distant that future I pictured was.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.210
No, because of that,

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:12.410
I want to wage a fight that wouldn't disgrace this name.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:14.550
This feeling of frustration I went through today...

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.670
I will never forget it...

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.830
You're admirable,

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:25.030
but you won't be able to accomplish your war relief, Alice.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:30.890
Farewell.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:38.940
Captain.

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:43.520
I was unable to protect any one thing in this incident.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:45.940
Am I right?

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:55.420
How many times must we endure this?

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:34.970
Mer-kun, I heard a princess from a country called Loderia has snuck into the country secretly.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:37.600
By the way, Machs,

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:39.060
what's a "French kiss"?

00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:41.920
Next time, "Rough Yet Delicious".

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:44.000
Come get us if you're not scared!
